		·· 18-11-2000 at 09:05 ·· ^<a href="#top">top</a></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
	<td bgcolor="#333333">
	    <font face="Verdana,Arial,Helvetica" size="-2"><br>
		Actually, SB will NOT be all about leveling. Yes, it will have the option to level, just like any other experience based game. However, Shadowbane is based around Seige Warfare. Who you ask is going to be the main fighting force? Grunts. The staple of any military force are always grunts. I highly doubt you will see level "60" type characters fighting hand in hand. These people will be your battle commanders and warlords, not armsmen. That's the difference between SB and EQ. There will ALWAYS be a need for lowbies. In EQ people don't like low levels. But since the BULK of EXP will come from PvP in SB, you can expect to see low levels more accepted, if not welcomed to the battlefield. --------- Colin-KGB Thanks for the Clearification on that Colin. It is good to see those that know how to have a True online gaming experience. A "True Online Game Experience" (TOGE) is where a player Finds an interesting online game, then reads all they can about it, learns all they can and then finally, starts to live it! Keeping informed about an Online game needs research and yes, you need to read! We have been told this from early childhood, reading is fundamental. If you do not research that which you want to learn about, your experience will be in vain. You might as well, look at the game box, say, wow cool, buy it and then start playing, only to discover it was not what you expected. And why? Because research was not done. We are all but students in this life, if one wants to be or not. The difference between being a "true student" and "just a student" is: Knowing how and where to seek reference so that you educate yourself enough to enjoy that which is around you. And you can't just look at pictures and read a few articles or from what others are saying. You need to get in there and research for yourself if you are to enjoy that which you seek. Of course, if you happen to know or spot a True Student then go ahead and listen to what they have to say. But it takes one to know one, and you will still need to research for yourself :) I would like to take this topic to our forums as it can be benificial to those that plan on playing Shadowbane. WTWYILAD!...CaScA
		<p><font size="1">
		<b>- <a href="mailto:CaSca@linkline.com">CaScA</a></b></font></font></td>
  </tr>
